{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Nitro group hydrogenation: catalyst and solvent screening",
  "notes": "Screening study for the hydrogenation of 4-chloro-2-nitrotoluene to the corresponding aniline in a parallel pressure reactor block. Seven process variables are screened in a 16-run resolution IV fractional factorial with four centre points (two with Pd/C in methanol, two with Pt/C in ethyl acetate). Conversion is measured by HPLC after 4 h; the hydrodechlorinated by-product (o-toluidine) is reported as HPLC area %, since it is difficult to purge downstream. The aim is to identify the few variables with a large effect on conversion and dechlorination before a response surface study.",
  "factors": [
